From 8a35e5198d510a90de4af56ef0a01f7a00e8ccfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:57:28 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_powerdevilprofilesconfig: state first, noun sections,
 async action support check
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Moved/renamed (UI only, same config keys, same backend):
- New first row "Right now: Using the "<state>" settings" (kcm.currentProfile). The AC/Battery/Low battery switch
  stays: the three power states are peers of one kind.
- "Suspend Session" split by topic into "Sleep" (when inactive, sleep mode), "Buttons and lid" (power button, lid,
  external monitor); "Display and Brightness" split into "Screen" (turn off, dim) and "Brightness" (screen, keyboard);
  "Other Settings" split into "Power profile" and "Commands". Order by use: Sleep, Screen, Brightness, Buttons and
  lid, Power profile, Commands. Sleep mode now sits next to the inactivity action it applies to.
- Toolbar "Configure Advanced Settings…" -> "Battery Levels and Charging…"; its page "Advanced Power Settings" ->
  "Battery Levels and Charging"; its "Other Settings" section -> "Media".
- "Choose run conditions" -> "Choose Run Conditions…" (opens a menu: title case + ellipsis).
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006 (state and common task first), HIG-015 (group by topic), HIG-023 (no blocking work),
HIG-057 (no "Advanced"). Page-design.md sections 2, 3, 6, 7.

Speed cause (code evidence): PowerKCM::PowerKCM() called asyncCall() and then reply.waitForFinished() once per
powerdevil action plugin with X-KDE-PowerDevil-Action-HasRuntimeRequirement, on the GUI thread, before the first
frame. Now a QDBusPendingCallWatcher per action; the action starts as unsupported (rows hidden) and
supportedActionsChanged() is emitted when the reply arrives; a failed call still means "supported" as before.
Only one ProfileConfig is instantiated (main.qml), not three, so there is nothing to defer there.
After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
